{"path":"cargo/guide/working-on-an-existing-project.html","title":"Working on an Existing Cargo Package","description":"If you download an existing package that uses Cargo, it’s really easy to get going.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"working-on-an-existing-cargo-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working on an Existing Cargo Package"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you download an existing "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#package","title":"\"package\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"text","value":"package"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that uses Cargo, it’s really easy to get going."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First, get the package from somewhere. In this example, we’ll use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"},{"type":"text","value":" cloned from its repository on GitHub:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ git clone https://github.com/rust-lang/regex.git\n$ cd regex"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To build, use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo build"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo build\n   Compiling regex v1.5.0 (file:///path/to/package/regex)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will fetch all of the dependencies and then build them, along with the package."}]}]}}
